Article 4 (Prohibition on Use of Subsidies for Purposes Other than Subsidized Projects)
(1) An educational foundation shall not use subsidies for purposes other than the purpose of grant specified in the notice of decision issued by the Minister of Education under Article 2 (2): Provided, That this shall not apply where prior approval has been obtained from the Minister of Education. <Amended on March 16, 1991; January 31, 2001; March 4, 2008; March 23, 2013>
(2) Where an educational foundation falls under any of the following subparagraphs, the Minister of Education may require it to return all or part of the subsidies granted: <Amended on March 16, 1991; January 31, 2001; March 4, 2008; March 23, 2013>
1. Where it violates paragraph (1);
2. Where it suspends or discontinues all or part of the subsidized project;
3. Where it fails to comply with a recommendation by the supervisory authority to amend its budget for the subsidized project;
4. Where it fails to comply with an order of the supervisory authority under the Private School Act or its Enforcement Decree;
5. Where continued subsidies are deemed inappropriate due to poor results of the subsidized project or it is deemed unlikely that the purpose of the subsidies will be achieved;
6. Where a report on the subsidized project is found to be false.
